abstract: >
  NurosOS is an open, modular, inspectable substrate for synthetic
  development — a runtime in which artificial organisms can be
  instantiated, developed, embodied, observed, measured, forked,
  replayed, and experimentally compared. The fundamental object is
  not MODEL but TRAJECTORY; not AGENT but DEVELOPING ORGANISM. The
  flagship Same Genome / Different World experiment demonstrates
  Computational Developmental Divergence: identical initial
  computational conditions producing divergent developmental states
  under different environmental histories. This is an observable
  computational fact, not evidence of consciousness.

  v0.4.0-alpha adds the HippoCore integration (10 phases): a
  MemoryEngine ABC with two implementations (DefaultMemoryContract
  for backward compatibility, HippoCoreMemory for episodic
  encoding, structured provenance, 5 replay policies, fast-to-slow
  consolidation, memory event emission for the developmental
  trajectory, and causal graph integration). 247 Python tests
  passing. NO LLM dependency.
